  "notes": [
   "The circuit image shows no breadboard; I used one mini breadboard (bb1) as the shared bus. SDA (A4) from both boards meets in column 5 and SCL (A5) in column 10. Each line has a 4.7k pull-up to a 3V3 rail strip fed from the reader's 3V pin. The catalogue breadboard is full-size, so mini-breadboard hole names are approximate.",
   "The manual lists 2 mini breadboards, but the image shows no use for the second. bb2 is included as a part with no connections.",
   "The manual lists 10 jumper wires. Only 6 are needed for the pictured circuit (3 on the reader, 2 on the writer, 1 for GND), so 6 are modelled.",
   "The image labels the reader supply pin '3V', which I mapped to the Nano Every '3V3' port. GND is mapped to 'GND1' on both boards.",
   "In the image, the teal A5 line (SCL) and the yellow A4 line (SDA) cross without connecting. Each pull-up resistor goes to its own line only.",
   "The manual says SDA is A4 and SCL is A5. Both boards are powered and programmed over USB from a computer, so each has a USB cable. The reader needs only power."
  ]
